<TUTORIAL>
	<ATTACK>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>WEAK STRIKE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        (PUNCH)</STR>
			<STR>                   (KICK)</STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>The weak strike is the most basic </STR>
			<STR>attack. Depending on your fight style,  </STR>
			<STR>you can also pull off some killer combos  </STR>
			<STR>by using multiple regular attacks. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you perform</STR>
			<STR>a weak punch or kick against </STR>
			<STR>your opponent. </STR>
			

			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>STRONG STRIKE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +       </STR>
			<STR>                   +       </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>Although they're slower to pull off,  </STR>
			<STR>strong attacks are more powerful than  </STR>
			<STR>regular attacks. Since they're slow, it's </STR>
			<STR>not a good idea to use them repeatedly.</STR>
			<STR>Save that for the regular moves. Also,</STR>
			<STR>you can use        as a modifier for other</STR>
			<STR>moves in different situations. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you perform</STR>
			<STR>a strong punch or kick against</STR>
			<STR>your opponent.</STR>
			

			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>8</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>57</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>RUNNING STRIKE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS       â†’          </STR>
			<STR>                  â†’    </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When your opponent is standing farther</STR>
			<STR>away from you, run towards him and </STR>
			<STR>press         or        to attack.</STR>
			<STR>Once mastered, this move can be </STR>
			<STR>great for getting back in the fight. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you perform</STR>
			<STR>a running strike against your</STR>
			<STR>opponent.</STR>
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>33</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>33</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>31</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>62</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>PURSUIT 1</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS                  /    </STR>
			<STR>                   +       /  </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>In this lesson, attack your opponent </STR>
			<STR>once so he loses balance. While he's </STR>
			<STR>stunned, punch or kick him with        or</STR>
			<STR>       to knock him down. You can  </STR>
			<STR>either use a regular or strong attack  </STR>
			<STR>to floor him.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you can knock </STR>
			<STR>your opponent down by stunning him, </STR>
			<STR>then striking him down. </STR>
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>65</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>89</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>65</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>89</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>146</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>6</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>PURSUIT 2</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        â†’       /  </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>You can use the pursuit grapple strike</STR>
			<STR>when you grapple an opponent who's</STR>
			<STR>off-balance from your first attack.</STR>
			<STR>In this lesson, your opponent will </STR>
			<STR>become off-balance from your first </STR>
			<STR>strike. While he's stunned from your </STR>
			<STR>blow, press        to grapple him. With</STR>
			<STR>your opponent grappled, you can strike</STR>
			<STR>5 times. But it's a timing issue, </STR>
			<STR>don't try to strike too quickly. </STR>
			<STR>It will take 5 strikes to give the </STR>
			<STR>finishing blow. The timing on this one </STR>
			<STR>is tricky. You'll need some skill.  </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will be complete when you </STR>
			<STR>get that fifth, finishing blow. </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>By the way, during this grapple, you </STR>
			<STR>can press         /        to shove. </STR>
			<STR>Shoving is another skill to add to </STR>
			<STR>your arsenal. Remember it.</STR>
			
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>65</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>92</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>8</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>54</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>19</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>52</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>19</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>78</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>WEAK GRAPPLE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        â†’        +     </STR>
			<STR>                   â†’        +     </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>This is a simple, regular grapple. While</STR>
			<STR>holding your opponent in a grapple, you </STR>
			<STR>can perform all sorts of moves from </STR>
			<STR>there, but keep it simple for now or </STR>
			<STR>you won't be able to finish the lesson. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you grapple </STR>
			<STR>your opponent and perform  a regular </STR>
			<STR>attack against him.</STR>

			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>68</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>97</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>68</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>97</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>STRONG GRAPPLE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +       â†’       +      </STR>
			<STR>                   +       â†’       +  </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>A hard grapple is essentially the same </STR>
			<STR>as a weak grapple, except now you </STR>
			<STR>need to use the         modifier to </STR>
			<STR>make it strong, just like regular </STR>
			<STR>and strong strikes.</STR>
			<STR>Aside from being stronger, another </STR>
			<STR>advantage of using a hard grapple is </STR>
			<STR>that the stronger grapple will last </STR>
			<STR>longer. Just like with weak grapples, </STR>
			<STR>you can get to a range of different </STR>
			<STR>moves from here, but just do a hard </STR>
			<STR>attack so you can finish the lesson. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you use a </STR>
			<STR>hard grapple to your opponent and then </STR>
			<STR>perform a strong attack against him.</STR>

			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>94</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>122</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>94</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>122</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>75</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>SHOVE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        â†’        +       /     </STR>
			<STR>                   +        â†’        +       /    </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>If you grapple your opponent during a </STR>
			<STR>fight, you can shove him away by</STR>
			<STR>pointing the      in any direction and </STR>
			<STR>pressing        . The main purpose of  </STR>
			<STR>shoving is to slam your opponent into a </STR>
			<STR>structure to perform enviromental  </STR>
			<STR>attacks. The distance of your shove  </STR>
			<STR>will depend on the amount of life your </STR>
			<STR>opponent has and  by whether your  </STR>
			<STR>initiating grapple is regular or strong.</STR>
			 <STR>Basically, you can shove your opponent</STR>
			<STR>with        , but sometimes if you use        ,</STR>
			<STR>an environmental attack will happen.</STR>
			<STR>If you only want to shove your opponent,</STR> 
                        <STR>press        instead.</STR>
			<STR>Shoving is a great move for gaining the</STR>
			<STR>upper hand in battles, so use it wisely.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you grapple </STR>
			<STR>then shove your opponent away.</STR>
			

			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>67</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>96</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>120</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>66</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>99</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>127</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>1</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>152</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>56</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>6</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>45</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>14</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>26</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>14</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>168</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>17</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>29</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>RUNNING GRAPPLE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        â†’     </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>To perform a running grapple, press      </STR>
			<STR>to run, then         to grapple your opponent.</STR>
			<STR>Depending on your fight style, the </STR>
			<STR>effects of this move will be different.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you perform</STR>
			<STR>a running grapple on your opponent.</STR>
			
			

			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>67</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>166</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>57</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>FORCE GRAPPLE</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS     </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When your opponent's on all fours, go up</STR>
			<STR>to him and press        to force him into a</STR>
			<STR>grapple. In this situation, you can either</STR>
			<STR>attack him or shove him around.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you can force</STR>
			<STR>your opponent on all fours into a grapple.</STR>
			
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>78</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>MOUNT</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        â†’        /       /       /</STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>All fighters can pound their opponent in</STR>
			<STR>the mount position, but only fighters who</STR>
			<STR>have learned the submission style can </STR>
			<STR>get into holds from mounts by pressing</STR>
			<STR>       . You can release your opponent by </STR>
			<STR>holding down        . </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you KO your</STR>
			<STR>opponent by mounting then pounding him.</STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>68</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>94</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>119</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>145</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>6</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>7</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>64</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
	</ATTACK>
	<DEFENCE>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>BLOCK</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>Allthough simple, this is one of the most</STR>
			<STR>important moves. This is your basic</STR>
			<STR>defensive stance. Don't think you won't</STR>
			<STR>need to use it, 'cause you will. You can</STR>
			<STR>use this to block your opponent's attack</STR>
			<STR>at anytime except during a reaction or</STR>
			<STR>if you're stunned. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you block </STR>
			<STR>an attack.</STR>
			
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>CATCH</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +        </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>If your opponent's attack hits you </STR>
			<STR>while in the catch position, you will </STR>
			<STR>successfully catch his attack. </STR>
			<STR>After you catch the strike, you'll</STR>
			<STR>automatically perform a counter attack.</STR>
			<STR>Keep in mind though, if you miss the</STR>
			<STR>catch, then you'll be an easier target.</STR>
			<STR>Catching is only effective on regular</STR>
			<STR>and strong attacks, not grapples.</STR>
			<STR>Be careful of your timing. </STR>
			<STR>This move takes some practice to get </STR>
			<STR>used to and  differs by fighting style. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you catch </STR>
			<STR>your opponent's attack.</STR>
			
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>GRAPPLE COUNTER</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        /       /     </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When you press        ,         , or        </STR>
			<STR>at the same time your opponent tries  </STR>
			<STR>to grapple you, you'll counterattack </STR>  
			<STR>his grapple. When you get it right, </STR>
			<STR>you'll avoid the grapple and attack </STR>
			<STR>your opponent. Some fighting styles </STR>
			<STR>can  do this move more easily than </STR> 
			<STR>others. Not only can you usethis during  </STR>   
			<STR>a normal grapple, but try it out with</STR>
			<STR>running grapples, forced grapples,</STR>
			<STR>and environmental attacks.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you counter </STR>
			<STR>your opponent's grapple.</STR>
			

			
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>61</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>87</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>77</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>104</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>142</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>BUMP</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS    </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When your opponent tries to throw you to</STR>
			<STR>the ground from a grapple, press         to</STR>
			<STR>get up faster and take less damage.</STR>
			<STR>The timing for this move is very </STR>
			<STR>important if you want to succeed. </STR>
			<STR>This move isn't  affected by your fight </STR> 
			<STR>style, so it's all up to your skill.  </STR>
			<STR>You won't be able to use this move in </STR>
			<STR>every attack where you hit the ground </STR>
			<STR>but you'll discover these as you fight. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you can</STR>
			<STR>successfully perform the bump move.</STR>
						

			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>152</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>ESCAPE</NAME>
			
			<STR>TAP          /      /        /        </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When you end up on the wrong end of </STR>
			<STR>a mount or submission move, tap         ,</STR>
			<STR>       ,          , or         as fast as possible.</STR>
			<STR>By filling the yellow bar on screen, </STR>
			<STR>you'll be able to escape. The bar will </STR>
			<STR>fill up at the speed you tap         ,        ,</STR>
			<STR>         , or        . </STR>
			<STR>This is the only way to escape from a  </STR>
			<STR>submission move. Remember in the   </STR>
			<STR>mount situation you could also try the   </STR>
			<STR>reverse move. Tapping is the most  </STR>
			<STR>surefire way to escape. This skill  </STR>
			<STR>isn't affected by any fight style,  </STR> 
			<STR>so it's all you. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you escape </STR>
			<STR>your opponent's move by tapping.</STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>30</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>55</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>80</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>105</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>150</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>4</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>4</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>30</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>4</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>69</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>7</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>128</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>7</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>156</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>8</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>5</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>8</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>43</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>REVERSAL</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +        </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>By pressing         +         with </STR>
			<STR>precise timing, you can get the  </STR>
			<STR>upper hand in grapple attacks, </STR>
			<STR>mounted pounding attacks, pursuit </STR>
			<STR>grapple attacks, and grapple counters. </STR>
			<STR>This move takes a lot of skill</STR>
			<STR>and practice. If you miss the catch,</STR>
			<STR>you'll get damaged and get a penalty</STR>
			<STR>on your escape meter.</STR>
			<STR>Basically, when the health gauge </STR>
			<STR>appears, try to escape by tapping the</STR>
			<STR>       +        . If you've only got a small</STR>
			<STR>amount of health left, you can hope</STR>
			<STR>for a miracle and try to reverse the</STR>
			<STR>pounding. The timing is tough, but  </STR>
			<STR>when you get it, it's worth it.  </STR>
			<STR>Otherwise, you can always escape </STR>
			<STR>by tapping. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you can</STR>
			<STR>reverse and be on top and start </STR>
			<STR>punishing your opponent rather than </STR>
			<STR>being down and taking damage. </STR>


			
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>59</BTNPOS>			
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>90</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>13</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>19</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>13</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>33</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
	</DEFENCE>
	<SPECIAL>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>REBOUND ATTACK</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS         â†’        /         </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>To perform a rebound attack, first you </STR>
			<STR>need to press         to run towards the </STR>
			<STR>ropes. Before you hit him, press         or</STR>
			<STR>       to rebound off the ropes and  </STR>
			<STR>attack your opponent. Any fighter can  </STR>
			<STR>perform a rebound attack against ropes,  </STR>
			<STR>but only martial artists can rebound  </STR> 
			<STR>off walls. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you  hit your</STR>
			<STR>opponent with a rebound attack.</STR>
			


			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>68</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>97</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>66</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>4</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>150</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>WEAPON </NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>PRESS        /   </STR>
			<STR>PRESS        +       /   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>PRESS        +   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>Weapons are available in most </STR>
			<STR>venues and can be extremely helpful </STR>
			<STR>in a fight. To pick up a weapon off the </STR>
			<STR>ground,  stand directly over it and</STR> 
			<STR>press         +         .</STR>
			<STR>You can use either strong or regular</STR>
			<STR>attack to attack with a weapon.</STR>
			<STR>When you want to drop your weapon,</STR>
			<STR>press         +         just like you did to</STR>
			<STR>pick it up. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end when you pick up,</STR>
                        <STR>use, then drop a weapon.</STR>
			

			
			
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>2</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>18</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>16</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>17</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>3</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>88</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>11</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>32</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>11</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>62</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>15</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>15</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>32</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>15</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>62</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>Env. ATTACK 1</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>In this lesson, your opponent's already</STR>
			<STR>leaning against a structure, so all you</STR>
			<STR>have to do is grapple him. In a real battle</STR>
			<STR>though, you have to put your opponent in</STR>
			<STR>that position yourself by grappling, then</STR>
			<STR>shoving him into a structure. Different</STR>
			<STR>environmental attacks happen in </STR>
			<STR>different places.  While going through </STR>
			<STR>venues, try to find the different moves. </STR>
			<STR>You can also try to initiate an</STR>
			<STR>environmental move by using a strong</STR>
			<STR>grapple on the stunned opponent, but</STR>
			<STR>there won't be a difference between</STR>
			<STR>the strong or normal grapples in this</STR>
			<STR>situation. By shoving then grappling your</STR>
			<STR>opponent in a crowd, you can execute</STR>
			<STR>double-team maneuvers. Environmental</STR>
			<STR>moves can really help you win a fight,</STR>
			<STR>so get familiar with the controls. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you perform an </STR>
			<STR>environmental attack on your opponent.</STR>
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>Env. ATTACK 2</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS    </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>This lesson starts with you leaning</STR>
			<STR>against a structure.  What you need </STR>
			<STR>to do is try to escape or change </STR>
			<STR>your position. Usually, you can just </STR>
			<STR>try to escape from the environmental</STR> 
			<STR>attack, but if you press         with</STR>
			<STR>precise timing, you'll be able to turn</STR>
			<STR>the tables. If you manage to pull this</STR>
			<STR>off, it'll be you in control and your</STR>
			<STR>opponent stunned against the structure.</STR>
			<STR>Remember though, you need exact </STR>
			<STR>timing to get this right, so take your </STR>
			<STR>time to learn it here. You can only </STR>
			<STR>use this move against structures, </STR>
			<STR>never crowd members.</STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you turn the</STR>
			<STR>tables in an environmental attack.</STR>
			

			
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE> <BTNPOS>34</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>7</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>111</BTNPOS>
			
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>Env. ATTACK 3</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        +   </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>When you're grappling your opponent </STR>
			<STR>and there's a structure behind you, you </STR>
			<STR>can perform an environmental attack by </STR>
			<STR>pointing the        towards the structure</STR>
			<STR>and pressing         .</STR>
			<STR>To properly initiate this move, you have</STR>
			<STR>to be at the right distance and angle </STR>
			<STR>from the structure.</STR>
			<STR>In this lesson, you start from a grappling</STR>
			<STR>state with a structure behind you, so </STR>
			<STR>just try to shove your opponent into the </STR>
			<STR>structure. Ring stages are special in </STR>
			<STR>that only wrestling experts can do </STR>
			<STR>these kinds of environmental attacks</STR>
 			<STR>by using rope.</STR>
			<STR>Note that you can only perform this </STR>
			<STR>kind of attack with structures, never </STR>
			<STR>with crowd members. </STR>
			<STR>The lesson will end after you perform</STR>
			<STR>an environmental attack using a</STR>
			<STR>structure behind you.</STR>
			
			
			
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>22</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>57</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>6</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>63</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>BLAZIN' TAUNT</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS        </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>In order to perform Blazin' moves, you</STR>
			<STR>need to activate Blazin' mode with a </STR>
			<STR>Blazin' Taunt. Once you fill your </STR>
			<STR>momentum meter, you'll be able to do a </STR> 
			<STR>Blazin' Taunt by pressing any direction </STR>
			<STR>on the       .</STR>
			<STR>Once in Blazin' mode, you'll do increased</STR>
			<STR>damage and ignore your injuries for </STR>
			<STR>a while.</STR>
			<STR>You'll also be able to do Blazin' moves.</STR>
			<STR>A regular taunt can be done by pressing</STR>
			<STR>        when your Blazin' bar isn't full.</STR>
			<STR>Regular taunts will help you fill the bar.</STR>
			<STR>This lesson will be over once you do a </STR>
			<STR>Blazin' Taunt to activate Blazin' mode.</STR>


			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>7</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>32</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>13</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>0</BTNPOS>
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>BLAZIN' MOVE 1</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS          â†’              </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>For those of you familiar with previous</STR>
			<STR>Def Jam games, you can still perform</STR>
			<STR>Blazin' moves in the same way.</STR>
			<STR>While in Blazin' mode, grapple your </STR>
			<STR>opponent and press any         to  do your </STR>
			<STR>default Blazin' move on your opponent.</STR>
			<STR>You can learn new Blazin' moves and </STR>
			<STR>assign a different move to each       </STR>
			<STR>at Stapleton's Athletics. </STR>
			<STR>New Blazin' moves are unlocked in</STR>
			<STR>Story mode as you progress and conquer</STR>
			<STR>fighters and venues.</STR>
			<STR>This lesson will be complete when you </STR>
			<STR>successfully perform a Blazin' move</STR>
			<STR>while in a grapple.</STR>

			
			
			<BTNTYPE>14</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
            		<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>73</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>6</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>110</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>9</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>154</BTNPOS>
			
		</ITEM>
		<ITEM>
			<NAME>BLAZIN' MOVE 2</NAME>
			
			<STR>PRESS         </STR>
			<STR> </STR>
			<STR>There's a second and simpler way to</STR>
			<STR>perform Blazin' moves. While in Blazin'</STR>
			<STR>mode, just get close to your opponent</STR>
			<STR>and press any direction on the         .</STR>
			<STR>This will activate your Blazin' move.</STR>
			<STR>Your opponent will still have a chance</STR>
			<STR>to block or counter your move, so</STR>
			<STR>have different moves ready by</STR>
			<STR>purchasing different Blazin' moves</STR>
			<STR>and assign them to different direction</STR>
			<STR>on the          at Stapleton Athletics.</STR>
			<STR>Different Blazin' moves do various </STR> 
			<STR>amounts of damage on certain </STR> 
			<STR>body parts. Some Blazin' moves can </STR>
			<STR>be activated while doing a dash, </STR>
			<STR>strike or other moves. </STR>
			<STR>This lesson will end when you </STR> 
			<STR>successfully perform a Blazin' move  </STR>
			<STR>by just using the        .</STR>
		
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>0</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>36</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>5</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>142</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>12</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>35</BTNPOS>
			<BTNTYPE>21</BTNTYPE><BTNLINE>20</BTNLINE><BTNPOS>78</BTNPOS>			
			
		</ITEM>
	</SPECIAL>
